This repository is a modern implementation/evolution of:
https://github.com/PjuralSzymon/growingnn

Core idea:
The framework trains neural networks whose architecture evolves during training.

The system has two major components:
1. Weight optimization (SGD/backpropagation)
2. Architecture orchestration

Architecture orchestration:
- The model structure changes during training.
- Architecture mutations occur periodically or when learning stagnates.
- Mutations are selected using Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS).
- The goal is balancing exploration of new architectures with exploitation of learned structures.

Model representation:
- The network is represented as a directed acyclic graph (DAG).
- Layers are graph nodes.
- Connections are directed edges.
- Residual and sequential connections are both supported.
- The graph must remain valid, acyclic, and connected.

Architecture mutations:
- Add/remove layers dynamically.
- Preserve residual structure when possible.
- Prefer non-destructive architecture updates.
- New layers should minimize disruption to learned knowledge.
- Architecture-changing logic must be modular and testable.

Training philosophy:
- Prefer simple SGD-based training logic.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction or overly complex frameworks.
- Preserve compatibility with standard PyTorch nn.Module behavior.
- Keep training logic separated from graph mutation logic.

Torch FX:
Use torch.fx for:
- graph tracing
- graph inspection
- graph transformation
- architecture mutation tooling

Reference:
https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/fx.html

Implementation guidance:
- Prefer PyTorch-native solutions.
- Prefer modular graph operations.
- Avoid hardcoded architectures.
- Keep layer operations composable.
- Preserve trainability after mutations.
- Add tests for graph mutations and architecture changes.